#atom_types amoeba-water-2003

!Version  Ref  Type  Mass    El  connections  Comment
!-------  ---  ----  ------  --  -----------  -------
 2003.1   1    OW    15.995  O   2            water O
 2003.1   1    HW    1.008   H   1            water H

#equivalence amoeba-water-2003

> The equivalent 'type' is the AMOEBA atom class carrying the valence and van der Waals parameters

!Version  Ref  Type  NonB  Bond  Angle  Torsion  OOP
!-------  ---  ----  ----  ----  -----  -------  ---
 2003.1   1    OW    OW    OW    OW     OW       OW
 2003.1   1    HW    HW    HW    HW     HW       HW

#buffered_14-7 amoeba-water-2003

> E = eps(ij) [(1 + delta)/(rho + delta)]^7 [(1 + gamma)/(rho^7 + gamma) - 2], rho = r/rmin(ij)
> rmin is the like-pair minimum distance; rmin(ij) and eps(ij) follow radiusrule and epsilonrule
> the hydrogen site sits on its bond at reduction x the bond length from the heavy atom

!Version  Ref  I   rmin   eps     reduction
!-------  ---  --  -----  ------  ---------
 2003.1   1    OW  3.405  0.11    1.0
 2003.1   1    HW  2.655  0.0135  0.91

#amoeba_bond amoeba-water-2003

> E = K2 dr^2 [1 + bond-cubic dr + bond-quartic dr^2], dr = R - R0

!Version  Ref  I   J   R0      K2
!-------  ---  --  --  ------  -----
 2003.1   1    HW  OW  0.9572  529.6

#amoeba_angle amoeba-water-2003

> E = K2 dTheta^2 [1 + angle-cubic dTheta + ... + angle-sextic dTheta^4] (dTheta in degrees, K2 per radian^2)
> Theta0_2 / Theta0_3 apply when the center carries 1 / 2 further hydrogens

!Version  Ref  I   J   K   K2     Theta0_1  Theta0_2  Theta0_3
!-------  ---  --  --  --  -----  --------  --------  --------
 2003.1   1    HW  OW  HW  34.05  108.5

#urey_bradley amoeba-water-2003

> E = K2 (S - S0)^2 on the I..K distance

!Version  Ref  I   J   K   S0      K2
!-------  ---  --  --  --  ------  -----
 2003.1   1    HW  OW  HW  1.5537  38.25

#atomic_multipole amoeba-water-2003

> Local frame from the bonded (or 1-3) atoms of the given types: Z X = z-then-x, -Z -X = bisector,
> Z -X -Y = z-bisect, -Z -X -Y = 3-fold, Z 0 = z-only, 0 = none; a fourth atom Y fixes the chirality
> dipole in e bohr, traceless quadrupole in e bohr^2 (atomic units, as in the papers and the Tinker files)

!Version  Ref  Type  Z    X    Y  Q         Dx        Dy   Dz        Qxx       Qxy  Qxz       Qyy       Qyz  Qzz
!-------  ---  ----  ---  ---  -  --------  --------  ---  --------  --------  ---  --------  --------  ---  -------
 2003.1   1    OW    -HW  -HW  0  -0.51966  0.0       0.0  0.14279   0.37928   0.0  0.0       -0.41809  0.0  0.03881
 2003.1   1    HW    OW   HW   0  0.25983   -0.03859  0.0  -0.05818  -0.03673  0.0  -0.00203  -0.10739  0.0  0.14412

#polarizability amoeba-water-2003

> thole = 0 selects charge-penetration damping; Group lists the atom types of the polarization group

!Version  Ref  I   alpha  thole  Group
!-------  ---  --  -----  -----  -----
 2003.1   1    OW  0.837  0.39   HW
 2003.1   1    HW  0.496  0.39   OW

#templates amoeba-water-2003

{
    "OW": {
        "2003.1": {
            "smarts": [
                "[O:1]([#1])[#1]"
            ],
            "description": "water oxygen"
        }
    },
    "HW": {
        "2003.1": {
            "smarts": [
                "[#1:1][O][#1]"
            ],
            "description": "water hydrogen"
        }
    }
}

#reference 1
@Author xnn
P. Ren and J. W. Ponder, Polarizable Atomic Multipole Water Model for Molecular
Mechanics Simulation, J. Phys. Chem. B 107, 5933-5947 (2003): Table 1 (all values).
Force-field definition (anharmonic coefficients, buffered 14-7 combining rules,
Thole damping, scale factors) from eqs 1-13 of the paper and from J. W. Ponder et al.,
J. Phys. Chem. B 114, 2549-2564 (2010), eqs 2-12. The Urey-Bradley distance is the
Table 1 value (1.5537 A); the text quotes 1.5326 A.

#end
